<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n31179" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἴρη</span></b>  (A), ἡ,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἴρω</span> 'speak') old 
			Ion.
		, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγορά</span>
			 or <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκκλησία</span>, <i>a place of
				assembly</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰράων προπάροιθε καθήμενοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					18.531
				</span></i>
			 (cf. Sch. ad loc. and <i><span class="en">
				<u>EM</u>
				483.3
			</span></i>); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιμίσγεται . . εἴρας ἐς ἀθανάτων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hes.
					<u>Th.</u>
					804
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Herm.
			</span></i> for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰρέας</span>): expld. by <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i> as 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐρώτησις, φήμη, κληδών</span>
			 (also written <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰρά, ἱρά</span>, by
			Gramm., cf. <i><span class="en">
				Apollon.
			</span></i><i>Lex.,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				EM
				475.12
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Suid.
			</span></i>).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
